{"url": "https://atmos.utah.edu/future/international.php", "final_url": "https://atmos.utah.edu/future/international.php", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-25", "text": "Department of Atmospheric Sciences - The University of Utah\nSkip to content\nSearch Site:\nPowered by\nSearch Campus:\nPowered by\nSearch Campus\nCampus Alert\nThe University of Utah\nDepartment of Atmospheric Sciences\nCollege of Mines and Earth Sciences\nAbout\nAbout Us\nPeople\nSEMINARS\nRESEARCH\nCOMMERCIAL APPLICATIONS\nDepartment forms & requests\nUndergraduate\nFuture\nUndergraduate\nMajor\nMinor\nCourses\nExperiential Learning\nInternships\nScholarships\nStudents with Children\nCareer Info\nAdvising\nGraduate\nFuture\nGraduate\nMS\nPhD\nCourses\nGraduate Student Guide\nTuition Benefit Program\nThe Graduate School\nUniversity Writing Center\nStudents with Children\nAdvising\nAir Quality\nCOVID-19 & Air Quality in Utah\nAQUARIUS\nDust\nU-ATAQ Lab\nHART\nLAIR\nMesoWest\nTRAX\nUtah DAQ\nAMSG\nWeather\nMesowest\nWeather Center\nWasatch Weather Weenies\nUtah Weather Center\nUtah Ski Weather\nAtmos Cameras\nGet Involved\nAMS at the U\nUtah Weather Center\nResearch Experiences For Undergraduates\nUtah Ski Weather\nCollege Epicenter\nAlumni & Friends\nAlumni and Friends\nDistinguished Alumni\nEndowments\nSearch\nReveal Menu\nReveal Menu\nMain Navigation\nMain Menu\nHome\nAbout\nAbout Us\nPeople\nSeminars\nResearch\nCommercial Applications\nDepartment forms & requests\nUndergraduate\nFuture\nUndergraduate\nMajor\nMinor\nCourses\nExperiential Learning\nInternships\nScholarships\nStudents with Children\nCareer Info\nAdvising\nGraduate\nFuture\nGraduate\nMS\nPhD\nCourses\nGraduate Student Guide\nTuition Benefit Program\nThe Graduate School\nUniversity Writing Center\nStudents with Children\nAdvising\nAir Quality\nCOVID-19 & Air Quality in Utah\nAQUARIUS\nDust\nU-ATAQ Lab\nHART\nLAIR\nMesoWest\nTRAX\nUtah DAQ\nWeather\nMesowest\nWeather Center\nWasatch Weather Weenies\nUtah Weather Center\nUtah Ski Weather\nAtmos Cameras\nGet Involved\nAMS at the U\nUtah Weather Center\nResearch Experiences For Undergraduates\nUtah Ski Weather\nCollege Epicenter\nAlumni & Friends\nAlumni and Friends\nDistinguished Alumni\nEndowments\nThings Of Interest\nNews Archive\nRecent Presentations\nUniversity Covid Central\nSeminars\nRecent Publications and Awards\nPet Pallet\nHome\nProspective\ncurrent page:\nInternational Students\nWe encourage applications to our graduate program from qualified candidates from nations\nworldwide. About 30% of the faculty, students and staff of the Department of Atmospheric\nSciences come from outside the United States, including Asia, Europe, South America,\nand Africa. The University hosts many programs for international students, and International Student and Scholar Services will assist you in many ways to become a successful member of the University. Further\ninformation can be found at the official web-site of the International Admissions Office.\nThe application procedure for international students is basically the same as for\nUS students. In addition, international student applicants must meet the Graduate\nSchool requirement of a score of 550 or more on the TOEFL examination or a score of\n6.5 or more on the IELTS examination. We understand that it is sometimes difficult\nto provide all the required documentation. If you need assistance please e-mail atmos-info@lists.utah.edu.\nMost of our applicants have degrees in atmospheric sciences/meteorology, environmental\nscience, physics, engineering, geophysics, or mathematics. We also encourage applicants\nwith expertise in chemistry, computer sciences and other relevant disciplines. At\nthe time of admission, international students should have at least earned a 4-year\nuniversity degree (equivalent to the Bachelor\u2019s degree) with a 75% (\"B\") average or\nbetter in a science or engineering discipline. Students in the final stages of completing\ntheir undergraduate program can submit an application for consideration prior to graduation,\nhowever admission is only permitted following the award of their 4-year university\ndegree. Nearly all of our graduate students start the program at the beginning of\nthe Fall semester in August.\nAtmospheric Sciences\nStewart Building\n270 S 1400 East Room E2108 ST\nSalt Lake City, UT 84112-0102\n801-581-6136\nStay in Touch\nFind Us\nContact Us\nWebmaster\nQuick Links\nCampus A to Z Index\nCampus Directory\nCampus Map\nShuttle Tracker\nCIS\nUMail\n@ The U\n\u00a9 2026 The University of Utah\nNondiscrimination & Accessibility\nDisclaimer\nPrivacy\nCredits & Attributions\nAbout the U\nMedia Contacts\nX\nFacebook\nInstagram\nYoutube\nLast Updated: 1/30/25", "links": [["Skip to content", "https://atmos.utah.edu/future/international.php#skip-link-target"], ["Campus Alert", "https://alert.utah.edu/"], ["The University of Utah", "https://www.utah.edu/"], ["Department of Atmospheric Sciences", "https://atmos.utah.edu/"], ["College of Mines and Earth Sciences", "https://cmes.utah.edu/index.php"], ["About", "https://atmos.utah.edu/future/international.php"], ["About Us", "https://atmos.utah.edu/about/index.php"], ["People", "https://atmos.utah.edu/about/people/index.php"], ["SEMINARS", "https://atmos.utah.edu/about/seminars.php"], ["RESEARCH", "https://atmos.utah.edu/about/research/index.php"], ["COMMERCIAL APPLICATIONS", "https://atmos.utah.edu/about/commercial-applications.php"], ["Department forms & requests", "https://atmos.utah.edu/forms/index.php"], ["Undergraduate", "https://atmos.utah.edu/future/international.php"], ["Future", "https://atmos.utah.edu/undergraduate/undergraduate-prospective.php"], ["Undergraduate", "https://atmos.utah.edu/undergraduate/index.php"], ["Major", "https://atmos.utah.edu/undergraduate/academics/degrees/major.php"], ["Minor", "https://atmos.utah.edu/undergraduate/academics/degrees/minor.php"], ["Courses", "https://catalog.utah.edu/#/Courses?expanded=Atmospheric%20Sciences"], ["Exp